From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:58:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 73/76] flashnext cuda: a MoE layer's router in two launches
 for passes of up to 16 rows behind TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUTE_FUSED

tf_route_logits_spread runs tf_route_logits_few's tiles and mma chains over 8 experts a one-warp block (65 blocks
instead of 17, each logit the same sums), and tf_route_topk_plan runs tf_route_topk's rows in eight groups side by
side, fn_ep_picks and experts.cu's one-block plan in one block: logits, top-k, own picks and plan in two launches
instead of four, with the same bytes. Off by default; route-rows checks both against the launches they replace.
